{"id":"mahabharata-7-022","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":22,"title":"द्वाविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 22 · The banners of the champions","summary":{"en":"At Dhritarashtra's request Sanjaya describes the horses, banners and chariots of the Pandava and Panchala heroes who rushed on Drona. Dhrishtadyumna rouses them as they gather around Bhima.","kn":"ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನ ಕೋರಿಕೆಯಂತೆ ದ್ರೋಣನ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗಿದ ಪಾಂಡವ, ಪಾಂಚಾಲ ವೀರರ ಕುದುರೆ, ಧ್ವಜ, ರಥಗಳನ್ನು ಸಂಜಯ ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಭೀಮನ ಸುತ್ತ ಸೇರಿದವರನ್ನು ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನ ಪ್ರೋತ್ಸಾಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र के अनुरोध पर संजय द्रोण पर टूटने वाले पाण्डव और पाञ्चाल वीरों के घोड़ों, ध्वजों और रथों का वर्णन करते हैं। भीम के चारों ओर जुटे वीरों को धृष्टद्युम्न प्रोत्साहित करते हैं।","te":"ధృతరాష్ట్రుని కోరిక మేరకు ద్రోణునిపై దూకిన పాండవ పాంచాల వీరుల గుర్రాలు, ధ్వజాలు, రథాలను సంజయుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు. భీముని చుట్టూ చేరిన వారిని ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుడు ప్రోత్సహిస్తాడు.","ta":"த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்க, த்ரோணரை நோக்கிப் பாய்ந்த பாண்டவ பாஞ்சால வீரர்களின் குதிரை, கொடி, தேர்களைச் சஞ்சயன் விவரிக்கிறான். பீமனைச் சுற்றித் திரண்டவர்களை த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னன் ஊக்குகிறான்.","ml":"ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രരുടെ ആവശ്യപ്രകാരം ദ്രോണരുടെ നേരെ പാഞ്ഞടുത്ത പാണ്ഡവ, പാഞ്ചാല വീരന്മാരുടെ കുതിരകളെയും കൊടികളെയും രഥങ്ങളെയും സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. ഭീമനെ ചുറ്റി അവർ ഒത്തുകൂടുമ്പോൾ ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നൻ അവരെ ഉണർത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.22; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"संशप्तकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Samshaptakavadha Parva (Slaying of the Samshaptakas)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सर्वेषामेव मे ब्रूहि रथचिह्नानि संजय ।\nये द्रोणमभ्यवर्तन्त क्रुद्धा भीमपुरोगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, tell me the chariot banners of all those, led by Bhima, who angrily advanced against Drona."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"ऋश्यवर्णैर्हयैर्दृष्ट्वा व्यायच्छन्तं वृकोदरम् ।\nरजताश्वस्ततः शूरः शैनेयः संन्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Vrikodara struggling, with horses the color of antelopes, brave Satyaki of the silver horses turned back to him."}},{"n":3,"text":"दर्शनीयास्तु काम्बोजाः शुकपत्रपरिच्छदाः ।\nवहन्तो नकुलं शीघ्रं तावकानभिदुद्रुवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Handsome Kamboja horses, covered with parrot-feather-green trappings, carried Nakula swiftly and charged at your men."}},{"n":4,"text":"कृष्णास्तु मेघसंकाशाः सहदेवमुदायुधम् ।\nभीमवेगा नरव्याघ्रमवहन्वातरंहसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Black horses like rain-clouds, fierce in speed and swift as wind, carried Sahadeva, tiger among men, with weapon raised."}},{"n":5,"text":"हेमोत्तमप्रतिच्छन्नैर्हयैर्वातसमैर्जवे ।\nअभ्यवर्तन्त सैन्यानि सर्वाण्येव युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the armies advanced toward Yudhishthira on horses covered with fine gold, swift as the wind."}},{"n":6,"text":"राज्ञस्त्वनन्तरं राजा पाञ्चाल्यो द्रुपदोऽभवत् ।\nजातरूपमयच्छत्रः सर्वैः स्वैरभिरक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Next after the king came the Panchala king Drupada, with a golden umbrella, guarded by all his own men."}},{"n":7,"text":"ललामैर्हरिभिर्युक्तैः सर्वशब्दक्षमैर्युधि ।\nराज्ञां मध्ये महेष्वासः शान्तभीरभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among the kings, that great archer of calm courage advanced with bay horses with white forehead marks, able to bear every sound in battle."}},{"n":8,"text":"तं विराटोऽन्वयात्पश्चात्सह शूरैर्महारथैः ।\nकेकयाश्च शिखण्डी च धृष्टकेतुस्तथैव च ।\nस्वैः स्वैः सैन्यैः परिवृता मत्स्यराजानमन्वयुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata followed him with brave great warriors, and the Kekayas, Shikhandi and Dhrishtaketu, each surrounded by their own troops, following the Matsya king."}},{"n":9,"text":"ते तु पाटलपुष्पाणां समवर्णा हयोत्तमाः ।\nवहमाना व्यराजन्त मत्स्यस्यामित्रघातिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of trumpet-flowers carried the Matsya king, slayer of foes, and shone as they went."}},{"n":10,"text":"हारिद्रसमवर्णास्तु जवना हेममालिनः ।\nपुत्रं विराटराजस्य सत्वराः समुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Swift horses the color of turmeric and wearing gold garlands quickly carried the son of King Virata."}},{"n":11,"text":"इन्द्रगोपकवर्णैस्तु भ्रातरः पञ्च केकयाः ।\nजातरूपसमाभासः सर्वे लोहितकध्वजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The five Kekaya brothers had horses the color of red velvet mites, all shining like gold, with red banners."}},{"n":12,"text":"ते हेममालिनः शूराः सर्वे युद्धविशारदाः ।\nवर्षन्त इव जीमूताः प्रत्यदृश्यन्त दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those brave men in gold garlands, all skilled in war, armored, appeared like rain-clouds pouring."}},{"n":13,"text":"आमपात्रनिभाकाराः पाञ्चाल्यममितौजसम् ।\nदान्तास्ताम्रारुणा युक्ताः शिखण्डिनमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tame horses of coppery red, like unbaked clay pots, carried the Panchala prince of boundless strength, Shikhandi."}},{"n":14,"text":"तथा द्वादशसाहस्राः पाञ्चालानां महारथाः ।\nतेषां तु षट्सहस्राणि ये शिखण्डिनमन्वयुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were twelve thousand Panchala great chariot-warriors, and of these six thousand followed Shikhandi."}},{"n":15,"text":"पुत्रं तु शिशुपालस्य नरसिंहस्य मारिष ।\nआक्रीडन्तो वहन्ति स्म सारङ्गशबला हयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses dappled like deer playfully carried the son of Shishupala, that lion among men, O sir."}},{"n":16,"text":"धृष्टकेतुश्च चेदीनामृषभोऽतिबलोदितः ।\nकाम्बोजैः शबलैरश्वैरभ्यवर्तत दुर्जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtaketu, bull of the Chedis, risen to great strength and hard to conquer, advanced with dappled Kamboja horses."}},{"n":17,"text":"बृहत्क्षत्रं तु कैकेयं सुकुमारं हयोत्तमाः ।\nपलालधूमवर्णाभाः सैन्धवाः शीघ्रमावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Swift Sindhu horses the color of straw-smoke carried the delicate Brihatkshatra, the Kekaya."}},{"n":18,"text":"मल्लिकाक्षाः पद्मवर्णा बाह्लिजाताः स्वलंकृताः ।\nशूरं शिखण्डिनः पुत्रं क्षत्रदेवमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Well-adorned horses born in Bahlika, with eyes like jasmine and the color of lotuses, carried the brave Kshatradeva, Shikhandi's son."}},{"n":19,"text":"युवानमवहन्युद्धे क्रौञ्चवर्णा हयोत्तमाः ।\nकाश्यस्याभिभुवः पुत्रं सुकुमारं महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heron-colored horses carried the young prince of Kashi, the delicate great warrior Abhibhu's son, in battle."}},{"n":20,"text":"श्वेतास्तु प्रतिविन्ध्यं तं कृष्णग्रीवा मनोजवाः ।\nयन्तुः प्रेष्यकरा राजन्राजपुत्रमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"White horses with black necks, swift as thought, obedient to the charioteer, carried Prativindhya, the prince, O king."}},{"n":21,"text":"सुतसोमं तु यं धौम्यात्पार्थः पुत्रमयाचत ।\nमाषपुष्पसवर्णास्तमवहन्वाजिनो रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of urad-flowers carried in battle Sutasoma, whom Arjuna asked of Dhaumya as a son."}},{"n":22,"text":"सहस्रसोमप्रतिमा बभूवुः\nपुरे कुरूणामुदयेन्दुनाम्नि ।\nतस्मिञ्जातः सोमसंक्रन्दमध्ये\nयस्मात्तस्मात्सुतसोमोऽभवत्सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was like a thousand Somas, born in the Kuru city called Udayendu amid the clamor of a Soma sacrifice; for that reason he was named Sutasoma."}},{"n":23,"text":"नाकुलिं तु शतानीकं शालपुष्पनिभा हयाः ।\nआदित्यतरुणप्रख्याः श्लाघनीयमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses like sala flowers and the young sun carried Nakula's son, the praiseworthy Shatanika."}},{"n":24,"text":"काञ्चनप्रतिमैर्योक्त्रैर्मयूरग्रीवसंनिभाः ।\nद्रौपदेयं नरव्याघ्रं श्रुतकर्माणमावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses with necks like peacocks, bound with golden harness, carried Shrutakarma, tiger among men, son of Draupadi."}},{"n":25,"text":"श्रुतकीर्तिं श्रुतनिधिं द्रौपदेयं हयोत्तमाः ।\nऊहुः पार्थसमं युद्धे चाषपत्रनिभा हयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of a blue-jay's wing carried Shrutakirti, Draupadi's son, treasury of learning, equal to Arjuna in battle."}},{"n":26,"text":"यमाहुरध्यर्धगुणं कृष्णात्पार्थाच्च संयुगे ।\nअभिमन्युं पिशङ्गास्तं कुमारमवहन्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tawny horses carried into the fight the young Abhimanyu, said to be one and a half times Krishna and Arjuna in virtue."}},{"n":27,"text":"एकस्तु धार्तराष्ट्रेभ्यः पाण्डवान्यः समाश्रितः ।\nतं बृहन्तो महाकाया युयुत्सुमवहन्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Large, huge-bodied horses carried Yuyutsu in battle, the one son of Dhritarashtra who took refuge with the Pandavas."}},{"n":28,"text":"पलालकाण्डवर्णास्तु वार्धक्षेमिं तरस्विनम् ।\nऊहुः सुतुमुले युद्धे हया हृष्टाः स्वलंकृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joyful, well-adorned horses the color of straw stalks carried the swift Vardhakshemi in that tumultuous battle."}},{"n":29,"text":"कुमारं शितिपादास्तु रुक्मपत्रैरुरश्छदैः ।\nसौचित्तिमवहन्युद्धे यन्तुः प्रेष्यकरा हयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Obedient horses with dark feet, with gold-leaf breast-plates, carried the young Sauchitti into battle."}},{"n":30,"text":"रुक्मपृष्ठावकीर्णास्तु कौशेयसदृशा हयाः ।\nसुवर्णमालिनः क्षान्ताः श्रेणिमन्तमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses like silk, sprinkled with gold on their backs, gentle, wearing golden garlands, carried Shrenimat."}},{"n":31,"text":"रुक्ममालाधराः शूरा हेमवर्णाः स्वलंकृताः ।\nकाशिराजं हयश्रेष्ठाः श्लाघनीयमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Excellent, well-adorned horses wearing golden garlands and shining like gold carried the praiseworthy king of Kashi."}},{"n":32,"text":"अस्त्राणां च धनुर्वेदे ब्राह्मे वेदे च पारगम् ।\nतं सत्यधृतिमायान्तमरुणाः समुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reddish horses carried Satyadhriti, who was master of the bow, of weapons and of the Brahma Veda, as he approached."}},{"n":33,"text":"यः स पाञ्चालसेनानीर्द्रोणमंशमकल्पयत् ।\nपारावतसवर्णाश्वा धृष्टद्युम्नमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of pigeons carried Dhrishtadyumna, commander of the Panchalas, who was made a portion of Drona's fate."}},{"n":34,"text":"तमन्वयात्सत्यधृतिः सौचित्तिर्युद्धदुर्मदः ।\nश्रेणिमान्वसुदानश्च पुत्रः काश्यस्य चाभिभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyadhriti, Sauchitti, mad for battle, Shrenimat, Vasudana and Kashya's son Abhibhu followed him."}},{"n":35,"text":"युक्तैः परमकाम्बोजैर्जवनैर्हेममालिभिः ।\nभीषयन्तो द्विषत्सैन्यं यमवैश्रवणोपमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With swift, excellent Kamboja horses in golden garlands they frightened the enemy army, like Yama and Kubera."}},{"n":36,"text":"प्रभद्रकास्तु पाञ्चालाः षट्सहस्राण्युदायुधाः ।\nनानावर्णैर्हयश्रेष्ठैर्हेमचित्ररथध्वजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Prabhadrakas of the Panchalas, six thousand with weapons raised, with horses of many colors and chariots with golden, variegated banners,"}},{"n":37,"text":"शरव्रातैर्विधुन्वन्तः शत्रून्विततकार्मुकाः ।\nसमानमृत्यवो भूत्वा धृष्टद्युम्नं समन्वयुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"shaking their foes with swarms of arrows and bows drawn wide, shared the same death-oath and followed Dhrishtadyumna."}},{"n":38,"text":"बभ्रुकौशेयवर्णास्तु सुवर्णवरमालिनः ।\nऊहुरग्लानमनसश्चेकितानं हयोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of tawny silk, with fine gold garlands, carried the unwearied Chekitana."}},{"n":39,"text":"इन्द्रायुधसवर्णैस्तु कुन्तिभोजो हयोत्तमैः ।\nआयात्सुवश्यैः पुरुजिन्मातुलः सव्यसाचिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kuntibhoja, Purujit, maternal uncle of Savyasachi, came with fine, well-controlled horses the color of rainbows."}},{"n":40,"text":"अन्तरिक्षसवर्णास्तु तारकाचित्रिता इव ।\nराजानं रोचमानं ते हयाः संख्ये समावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of the sky, spangled as if with stars, carried the radiant king in battle."}},{"n":41,"text":"कर्बुराः शितिपादास्तु स्वर्णजालपरिच्छदाः ।\nजारासंधिं हयश्रेष्ठाः सहदेवमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dappled horses with dark feet and golden-net coverings carried Sahadeva, son of Jarasandha."}},{"n":42,"text":"ये तु पुष्करनालस्य समवर्णा हयोत्तमाः ।\nजवे श्येनसमाश्चित्राः सुदामानमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of lotus stalks, swift as hawks and varied in color, carried Sudaman."}},{"n":43,"text":"शशलोहितवर्णास्तु पाण्डुरोद्गतराजयः ।\nपाञ्चाल्यं गोपतेः पुत्रं सिंहसेनमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of a hare's blood, with white lines rising on them, carried Simhasena, the Panchala son of Gopati."}},{"n":44,"text":"पाञ्चालानां नरव्याघ्रो यः ख्यातो जनमेजयः ।\nतस्य सर्षपपुष्पाणां तुल्यवर्णा हयोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The tiger among the Panchalas, famed Janamejaya, had horses the color of mustard flowers."}},{"n":45,"text":"माषवर्णास्तु जवना बृहन्तो हेममालिनः ।\nदधिपृष्ठाश्चन्द्रमुखाः पाञ्चाल्यमवहन्द्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Swift, large horses the color of urad beans, in gold garlands, curd-backed and moon-faced, quickly carried the Panchala."}},{"n":46,"text":"शूराश्च भद्रकाश्चैव शरकाण्डनिभा हयाः ।\nपद्मकिञ्जल्कवर्णाभा दण्डधारमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses like reed stalks, the color of lotus filaments, carried the Danadhara, the brave Bhadrakas."}},{"n":47,"text":"बिभ्रतो हेममालाश्च चक्रवाकोदरा हयाः ।\nकोसलाधिपतेः पुत्रं सुक्षत्रं वाजिनोऽवहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses with gold garlands and bellies like chakravaka birds carried Sukshatra, the son of the lord of Kosala."}},{"n":48,"text":"शबलास्तु बृहन्तोऽश्वा दान्ता जाम्बूनदस्रजः ।\nयुद्धे सत्यधृतिं क्षैमिमवहन्प्रांशवः शुभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tall, auspicious dappled horses, tame and with Jambunada gold garlands, carried Satyadhriti Kshaimi in battle."}},{"n":49,"text":"एकवर्णेन सर्वेण ध्वजेन कवचेन च ।\nअश्वैश्च धनुषा चैव शुक्लैः शुक्लो न्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a single color in banner, armor, horses and bow, all white, the white warrior advanced."}},{"n":50,"text":"समुद्रसेनपुत्रं तु सामुद्रा रुद्रतेजसम् ।\nअश्वाः शशाङ्कसदृशाश्चन्द्रदेवमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Moon-like Samudra horses carried Chandradeva, son of Samudrasena, who had the fire of Rudra."}},{"n":51,"text":"नीलोत्पलसवर्णास्तु तपनीयविभूषिताः ।\nशैब्यं चित्ररथं युद्धे चित्रमाल्यावहन्हयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of blue lotuses, decorated with gold, carried the Shaibya Chitraratha in battle, wearing varied garlands."}},{"n":52,"text":"कलायपुष्पवर्णास्तु श्वेतलोहितराजयः ।\nरथसेनं हयश्रेष्ठाः समूहुर्युद्धदुर्मदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of pea-flowers, with white and red lines, carried Rathasena, mad for war."}},{"n":53,"text":"यं तु सर्वमनुष्येभ्यः प्राहुः शूरतरं नृपम् ।\nतं पटच्चरहन्तारं शुकवर्णावहन्हयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king said to be the bravest of all men, slayer of Patachchara, was carried by parrot-colored horses."}},{"n":54,"text":"चित्रायुधं चित्रमाल्यं चित्रवर्मायुधध्वजम् ।\nऊहुः किंशुकपुष्पाणां तुल्यवर्णा हयोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of kimshuka flowers carried Chitrayudha, with his varied weapons, garlands, armor and banner."}},{"n":55,"text":"एकवर्णेन सर्वेण ध्वजेन कवचेन च ।\nधनुषा रथवाहैश्च नीलैर्नीलोऽभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a single color in banner, armor, bow and chariot-horses, all blue, the blue warrior advanced."}},{"n":56,"text":"नानारूपै रत्नचित्रैर्वरूथध्वजकार्मुकैः ।\nवाजिध्वजपताकाभिश्चित्रैश्चित्रोऽभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The varied one advanced with varied jeweled armor, banner and bow, and horses, standards and pennants of many kinds."}},{"n":57,"text":"ये तु पुष्करपत्रस्य तुल्यवर्णा हयोत्तमाः ।\nते रोचमानस्य सुतं हेमवर्णमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of lotus leaves carried the golden-hued son of Rochamana."}},{"n":58,"text":"योधाश्च भद्रकाराश्च शरदण्डानुदण्डजाः ।\nश्वेताण्डाः कुक्कुटाण्डाभा दण्डकेतुमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses like white eggs, like hen's eggs, carried Dandaketu, with warriors who were Bhadrakaras, born of arrow-shafts."}},{"n":59,"text":"आटरूषकपुष्पाभा हयाः पाण्ड्यानुयायिनाम् ।\nअवहन्रथमुख्यानामयुतानि चतुर्दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses the color of atarushaka flowers carried fourteen thousand chief chariot-warriors who followed the Pandyas."}},{"n":60,"text":"नानारूपेण वर्णेन नानाकृतिमुखा हयाः ।\nरथचक्रध्वजं वीरं घटोत्कचमुदावहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Horses of many colors and of varied faces carried the hero Ghatotkacha, whose banner bore a chariot wheel."}},{"n":61,"text":"सुवर्णवर्णा धर्मज्ञमनीकस्थं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nराजश्रेष्ठं हयश्रेष्ठाः सर्वतः पृष्ठतोऽन्वयुः ।\nवर्णैश्चोच्चावचैर्दिव्यैः सदश्वानां प्रभद्रकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Golden-colored, excellent horses of many fine colors followed everywhere behind the righteous king Yudhishthira, best of kings, stationed in his division, and the Prabhadrakas were with them."}},{"n":62,"text":"ते यत्ता भीमसेनेन सहिताः काञ्चनध्वजाः ।\nप्रत्यदृश्यन्त राजेन्द्र सेन्द्रा इव दिवौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Led by Bhima, with golden banners, they appeared, O king of kings, like the gods with Indra."}},{"n":63,"text":"अत्यरोचत तान्सर्वान्धृष्टद्युम्नः समागतान् ।\nसर्वाण्यपि च सैन्यानि भारद्वाजोऽत्यरोचत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna outshone all of them gathered there, and Bharadvaja's son outshone all the armies."}}]}]}